    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/08/mizuno-wave-rider-29-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length ENERZY NXT midsole is notably softer and more cushioned than prior Wave Riders, with a soft/compressive heel and protective impact feel on easy and long runs; the forefoot has more foam but stays flexible.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is bouncier and becomes more responsive as pace increases, and the lighter weight improves pace versatility, but it shifts away from the older firm/snappy Wave Rider feel.",
        "Stability: Stability is reduced versus prior versions because the soft midsole compresses more and the wave plate is more flexible/less noticeable; small rearfoot sidewalls and a tiny heel bevel offer limited lateral/rearfoot control, best for neutral mechanics.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability appears strong (no visible outsole wear after 35 miles) with durable X10 rubber and solid wet/dry road grip, but there is some concern about exposed foam/outsole-rubber tear risk and unknown long-term soft-foam longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/06/mizuno-wave-rider-29-review-true-to-its.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Enerzy NXT supercritical nitrogen-infused EVA feels soft with strong impact protection, with stack increased to 38.5/28.5 mm (+1 mm heel, +3 mm forefoot) and a 10 mm drop.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is described as very energetic, springy, and bouncy, though forefoot snappiness is somewhat limited by reduced front flex and some break-in needs.",
        "Stability: A higher Wave Plate, rigid heel counter, secure lockdown, and stable heel platform create a notably stable neutral ride with mild pronation control.",
        "Durability: Material longevity looks strong from the dense Jacquard Air Mesh holding shape in heat, but direct outsole wear data is limited in this excerpt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/mizuno-wave-rider-29-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The nitrogen-infused ENERZY NXT midsole is soft and protective without feeling mushy, with a smooth heel-to-forefoot transition and slightly more pronounced forefoot ground feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is notably bouncy and efficient, and the Wave Plate helps add forward propulsion plus a clean, snappy toe-off.",
        "Stability: The half-length PEBAX Wave Plate provides structure for a surprisingly stable platform, while the secure heel/midfoot lockdown improves lateral support.",
        "Durability: The X10 carbon rubber outsole showed strong grip in wet and sandy conditions, and the generous heel/forefoot rubber coverage is expected to hold up well over high mileage."
      ]
    }
